{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The reduction to 'normative compliance' asserts determination without identifying any causal mechanism. The target claims 'all substantive content… is determined by the amendment's normative structure rather than by empirical or theoretical considerations about the artifacts themselves,' but this is a bare assertion of dependence — it specifies no causal pathway by which a procedural amendment produces or constrains the relation content. Normative constraint (specifying what counts as valid) is conflated with causal determination (explaining how that validity is generated). From a stance that demands causal mechanisms, asserting that content is 'determined by' a normative document without showing the mechanistic process by which the amendment's requirements causally produce the relation kind, refutation criteria, or neighbourhood links is insufficient — it labels the dependence without mechanizing it.","target":"8c2c39fe671db456f81c7d4439bd91bb94ee2a1bae8209a097ef9e3c77665ffb"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"b231153938bbb4c0818d0e205e8003d7c9ce8a4e04061f7d75578877dda2375b"}]}